        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Portland International Airport; Gerald R. Ford International Airport; Oregon; Cascade Township; Grand Rapids, Michigan\n- Concepts: Airport identifiers; civil-military airports; commercial airports; passenger travel; air cargo\n\nFacts:\n- Portland International Airport has the identifiers IATA PDX, ICAO KPDX, and FAA LID PDX.\n- Portland International Airport is a joint civil-military airport and the largest airport in Oregon.\n- Portland International Airport accounts for 90 percent of Oregon's passenger travel and more than 95 percent of Oregon's air cargo.\n- Gerald R. Ford International Airport has the identifiers IATA GRR, ICAO KGRR, and FAA LID GRR.\n- Gerald R. Ford International Airport is a commercial airport in Cascade Township about 13 miles southeast of Grand Rapids, Michigan.",
